  "_about": "How much each news outlet's reporting can be trusted, 0-100, from two outside raters (checked 2026-11-10). MBFC (mediabiasfactcheck.com) factual score 0 best to 10 worst -> 100 - 10 x score (label only: its middle value). Ad Fontes (adfontesmedia.com) reliability 0-64 -> 100 x (R - 8) / 40, capped 0-100 (48, the bottom of its 'original fact reporting' band, = 100). Rating = average of the two where both rate an outlet, else the one that does, capped at 99. Outlets neither rates get 'unrated'. Government and central-bank sources aren't media and get no rating: their headlines are labelled 'official' (a reliable record of what was said, still one side's claim). Only accuracy/reliability is used, never the bias scores. To change a rating, update its inputs and re-apply.",
